{"text": "CADWELL SANFORD DEIBERT & GARRY tie\n\nLAWYERS\ndoe W, Cadwell Telephone\nSteven W, Sanford River Centre (605) 336-0828\nDouglas M. Deibert 200 East 10\u201d Street, Suite 200\nWilliam C. Garry Sioux Falls, South Dakota 57104 Fax\nScott Perrenoud* (605) 336-6036\nStephen C. Landon Malling Address:\nBrett A. Lovrien** P.O. Box 2498 Writer's E-Mail Address\nJames S. Simko Sioux Falts, South Dakota 57101 slandon@oadlaw.com\nShawn M. Nichols\nKristi M. Laber\nMelissa R. Jelen\nAlex M. Hagen\n* Also admitted in iowa\n' Also admitted in Minnesots\nFebruary 3, 2017\nLora Hubbel\n510 W. 24\" Street, #2\nSioux Falls, SD 57105\n\nRe: NOTICE TO CEASE AND DESIST FROM LIBELOUS STATEMENTS\nMs. Hubbel:\n\nWe represent Mike Huether, who, as you know, is currently the Mayor of Sioux Falls.\nYour recent Facebook posts and Twitter tweets asserting that Mayor Huether is \u201ctreasonous\u201d\nbecause he has \u201cbrought in\u201d and \u201cappointed to a position of influence\u201d and \u201cgiven authority to\u201d\nTanzeea (whom you also refer to in places as \u201cTaneeza\u2019) Islam are completely false. Your\ncharacterization of Mayor Huether as \u201cselling our state to the Islamic cause\u201d and being a \u201clover\u201d\nof the Muslim Brotherhood are also completely false. Further, by posting your false statements in\nassociation with a picture of an entirely different person, you are intentionally misleading all who\nview the post in an attempt to wrongfully harm Mayor Huether.\n\nYour intentionally false public statements about Mayor Huether are libel and you are\nhereby advised to immediately CEASE and DESIST from making such statements. You are\nfurther advised to take immediate action to remove the posts and tweets to prevent further wrongful\ndissemination of the false and harmful statements.\n\nWhile you have the same right as all citizens to agree or disagree-with public figures, such\nas Mayor Huether, and to state your disagreement publicly if you wish, you do not have the right\nto engage in a deliberate campaign to spread false information as a means of harming another\ncitizen, even one who is in public office. Your conduct is unlawful and must stop.\nVery truly yours,\nCADWELL SANFO! EIBERT & GARRY, LLP\nStephen C. Landon\n\nc: Mike Huether",
